Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-08-2000||08:49 PM||||  Has anyone attempted or been successfull with a 4.3L swap? I need feedback.<P> Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-08-2000||09:21 PM||||Awhile back, Batboy mentioned that he was going to do this swap.  Might wanna shoot him an email...||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||04-08-2000||10:08 PM||||Yes, I had thought about a 4.3 swap since I could get an engine given to me from my Dad. But the 4.3 needs a complete rebuild, so I'm back to looking for a 1987 2.5 engine, especially now that I have another truck project.<P>However, Squid has most of the parts gathered up and seems to be on top of what's needed for the swap. You might ask him. We have a couple old topics here on the Forum too. The 4.3 V6 is a 350 small block minus 2 cylinders. You need the basic Chevy V8 conversion kit from V8 Archie's or another similar outfit. The custom flywheel is one of the big hurdles in this swap.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||04-09-2000||02:59 PM||||I was thinking that this might be an interesting swap, too. It seems like almost as much of a pain in the a$$ as a V-8 swap, though. <BR>One word of caution... The early 4.3 V-6s vibrated pretty badly. The later ones have balance shafts. I don't know how much of an improvement this made. I have a 92 Sonoma with a 4.3 (no balance shaft) and a 5-speed. It vibrates enough to be annoying. It doesn't actually shake the truck, but at certain RPMs, it resonates through the driveline (felt in the shifter). If you used a V-8 kit with solid mounts, it might be *really* unpleasant. Just my $.02.<P>If you try this swap, please let us know how it works.||||reg||1
